    "open_questions": [
      "Going Underground (1980): no drum tab of any kind exists on Songsterr and no transcription was found; the record is too dense to read by beat-tracking. Not written as a song.",
      "Down in the Tube Station at Midnight: the only tab is machine-made; check its bars against the record, and the heartbeat effect against the drums.",
      "His kits by year: a chrome-wrapped kit on Top of the Pops in March 1980, the white Premier with Paiste cymbals of the 1980s (Christie's), the 'Great White' kit of the Malice and Funeral Pyre videos. Makes and sizes before 1980 not found.",
      "Read his autobiography (That's Entertainment, 2015) and The Jam: Our Story (1994) for his own account of his parts, Funeral Pyre's rolls and Precious.",
      "Who cites him: no drummer naming him as an influence was found."
    ]
  },
