    "roles": ["band_member", "touring", "producer"],
    "summary": "The Jam's drummer from its start at Sheerwater Secondary School in Woking in 1972 to its end in December 1982: six albums, eighteen top-40 singles and four number ones with Paul Weller and Bruce Foxton. Self-taught, first on a stack of Chuck Berry records Weller handed him; Ian Paice, John Bonham and Ringo Starr his models. Plain, driving eighths with the kick pushing the 'and's, the open hat and crashes marking the words, and 'bursts of snare' (MOJO); by Sound Affects the Off the Wall soul in his playing, by Town Called Malice a Motown stomp. Later Time UK, production, From the Jam (2007-2009). He died in Woking in February 2025."
  },
